I think you should be able to polish, or buff up, items by using a
towel.  However, the only "polished" item I am aware of is the polished
silver shield, and there's no way of obtaining a non-polished one.

So here's my plan:  Rubbing a metallic shield with a towel should take
several turns, the end result being one of the following:

80% : nothing
10% : damage the shield (corrode it, or un-rustproof it)
5%  : destroy the towel
5%  : turn shield into a "shiny shield"

A shiny shield would provide reflection just like a polished silver one
does, but when next rusted/corroded, it reverts to being a normal
shield.

This would provide a means for a desperate player, with a lot of other
resources, to get hold of some temporary reflection.

